    "difficulty": "MODERATE",
    "stem": "Find \\(\\int \\sqrt{x^2 + 2x + 5}\\,dx\\).",
    "solution": "Note that \\(\\int \\sqrt{x^2 + 2x + 5}\\,dx = \\int \\sqrt{(x+1)^2 + 4}\\,dx\\). Put \\(x + 1 = y\\), so that \\(dx = dy\\). Then \\(\\int \\sqrt{x^2 + 2x + 5}\\,dx = \\int \\sqrt{y^2 + 2^2}\\,dy = \\frac{1}{2}\\,y\\sqrt{y^2 + 4} + \\frac{4}{2}\\log\\left|\\,y + \\sqrt{y^2 + 4}\\,\\right| + C\\) [using 7.6.2 (ii)] \\(= \\frac{1}{2}(x+1)\\sqrt{x^2 + 2x + 5} + 2\\log\\left|\\,x + 1 + \\sqrt{x^2 + 2x + 5}\\,\\right| + C\\)."
  },
