    "stem": "Find \\(\\int \\sqrt{3 - 2x - x^2}\\,dx\\).",
    "solution": "Note that \\(\\int \\sqrt{3 - 2x - x^2}\\,dx = \\int \\sqrt{4 - (x+1)^2}\\,dx\\). Put \\(x + 1 = y\\) so that \\(dx = dy\\). Thus \\(\\int \\sqrt{3 - 2x - x^2}\\,dx = \\int \\sqrt{4 - y^2}\\,dy = \\frac{1}{2}\\,y\\sqrt{4 - y^2} + \\frac{4}{2}\\sin^{-1}\\frac{y}{2} + C\\) [using 7.6.2 (iii)] \\(= \\frac{1}{2}(x+1)\\sqrt{3 - 2x - x^2} + 2\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x+1}{2}\\right) + C\\)."
  },
